rem  Version : v188   build 2026-11-28 - the build finds your shader tags wherever they sit
rem            The compile script looked for each shader tag in two places only,
rem            tags\ and tags\<item>\, and called the rest missing. Halo's own tags are
rem            not laid out that way: a character's sit under characters\<name>\, which
rem            is exactly where this item's are. So every run since that check was added
rem            said "nothing was compiled, on purpose" over a tag that was right there,
rem            and the model tag on disk stayed the one an earlier build wrote. The arms,
rem            the pose and the white face the game showed were that older model, however
rem            many times the item had been rebuilt since - and the face was white for the
rem            second reason too, the empty reference baked into it.
rem            The check now indexes every shader_model under tags\ and matches the name,
rem            which is the test tool.exe itself makes: a shader is found by its name, in
rem            whatever folder it sits. A missing one is still named and still stops the
rem            model compiling - an empty shader must never be baked - but a tag under
rem            characters\<item>\ now counts, and so does one anywhere else.
rem            "Check the shaders.bat" had the same blind spot the other way round: it
rem            looked for <item>.gbxmodel in tags\<item>\ only, so a model tag sitting in
rem            tags\characters\<item>\ was reported as never compiled. It now finds the
rem            newest copy anywhere under tags\ and prints the path it read.
rem            Nothing about the model changed in this build: same .jms, same node block,
rem            same three material names, same pose.
